<font class="option" color="#363636"><b>How to make Fear and Hate Fun</b></font><br>
<font class="content">Posted On 2002-02-14 10:47:32 by <a href="http://">Charoth</a></td></tr></table></td></tr></table><br>Thats right, Fear and Hate, the planes we all aspired for once, spent days in, not hours and if you didn't die at least 5 times, it wasn't a real raid. We strolled into Fear Tuesday, to take out what we could take out, but upon zoning in the plane was empty, hmm, that would kind of put a damper on things, so we had a GM repop the zone while our little force was in the safe spot (Read More)<BR><BR>Then from at least 5 different angles the mobs started advancing and the fun began, and about 5 to 10 minutes later (who can ever keep track of such things) we thought we were going to get a rest, but our suicidal puller Effix had other ideas. Long story short, the only rest we had was when he went LD and I got to pull, ok maybe I took too many lessons form him, but 1 mob at a time isn't fun, 2 is boring, 4+ is where the action is.<br /><br />Anyway, Draco and his 3 Golem poker buddies went down, warrior/shaman epic pieces fell, some rainbow shield of goodness, the robe that used to drop off cazic and the amulet of necropolence (forgive the memory, I guess I should start to write things down).<br /><br />As for Hate, our goal was the Magi staff, which of course didn't drop (first one in like 10 magi's since they upped the drop rate or something), we got alot of other hate armor (snore) and another warrior piece (go green scaleless warriors!). So, 2 old school days for OoO, and to answer my question the only way to make the old planes fun, is to have Effix pull more then 5 at a time non stop while killing all your clerics, all your enchanters, and himself in the process. Now that, is fun.<br /><br />This is what happens when you give your guild the skelly amulet for a few minutes, courtesy of the Lady Eloine : <br /><br /><A HREF="tempimages/skeleton.jpg" TARGET="_blank"><IMG SRC="tempimages/skeleton.jpg" WIDTH="400" BORDER="0"></A><br />(click to enlarge)</td></tr></table></td></tr></table><br>


